	(text "BUS TERMINATION - fit BOTH shunts for an end-of-bus node.\nRemove BOTH for a mid-bus drop; never fit only one."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 179.832 183.642 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "77d39e2c-1003-4adc-80c6-7207c2ff8852")
	)
	(text "The purpose of this circuit is to isolate the CAN from the rest of the PCB.\nAlso provide optional 24VDC over the CAN bus < 3 meters.\n\n  1 - Provide CAN isolation between the STM32 CAN pins and the CAN bus\n  2 - 24VDC into CAN_V+ RJ45 pin 8. Can be turned ON/OFF with switch.\n  3 - Limit current on CAN_V+ to 0.87A, protecting 22AWG CAT6 wires\n  4 - Reverse polarity protection\n  5 - CAN termination resistors"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 193.294 26.162 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "8c11b4b0-d8ba-46aa-8d7f-c7328b78f527")
	)
	(text "Q9 - Services the switch, turn CAN_V+ on/off\nQ10 - reverse polarity + reverse current blocking FET\nQ11 - fast gate pull-down for Q10"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 54.356 44.45 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "951b6631-b979-400f-b75d-46f50f082339")
	)
	(text "Ensure that GND_ISO (Pin 18) is connected \nby a trace to the other GND_ISO pin (Pin 20) \non the inside (device side) of the C88 100 nF \ncapacitor"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 114.046 106.68 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "a9d3e7e4-7e53-4a74-b4f3-1a1ad74e28d4")
	)
	(text "Q9 = P-FET high-side switch for CAN_V+.\nSW3 closed -> R101/R102 hold the gate at\n12 V, VGS = -12 V, Q9 ON (LED5 lights).\nSW3 open -> R101 pulls gate to source,\nVGS = 0, Q9 OFF."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 144.78 40.386 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "acedfc27-4558-4cb5-ab1d-10ffc0029f35")
	)
	(text "24V CAN BUS POWER  ->  CAN_V+ = RJ2 pin 8\n(24 V return on pin 7, its CAT5 pair mate)\nThe 24 V supply MUST be floating - its negative\nbecomes CAN_GND, the isolated side of the\nADM3057E barrier. Earthing it defeats isolation.\nQ10 is the reverse-blocking FET (S=IN_SYS, D=IN,\nG=BGATE); Q11 is the fast gate pull-down from\nDRV. That pair gives reverse-polarity AND\nreverse-current blocking. C95/D41 sit on OUT, so\na reversed supply cannot forward-bias the TVS\nor the electrolytic."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.272 167.894 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e43f1518-6fab-45f7-8bfe-5f7a105ee9c8")
	)
	(text "STM32 to CAN"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 43.434 18.542 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 5.08 5.08)
			)
		)
		(uuid "f2eb320e-9f63-412f-b399-e83965edadab")
	)
	(text "Place D42 close to IN_SYS"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 90.932 92.71 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "f4f210e8-7684-4f45-b23a-77b7c6270969")
	)
